# Template for .env: local paths of the external tools and corpora used by the opt-in tests.
# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and fill in what you have.
#
# A test run uses only local resources unless it selects external ones by name:
#   uv run --env-file .env pytest --external-tools=all --external-corpora=all   (validation)
#   uv run --env-file .env pytest --external-tools=yosys,sby                    (some tools)
#   uv run pytest                                                               (local only)
# The variables below say WHERE a resource is; the switches say WHETHER a run uses it. A
# selected resource whose variable is unset or invalid stops the run with a usage error.
# Variables already set in the shell take precedence over this file.
#
# Format (uv's dotenv parser): KEY='value'. Keep the single quotes: unquoted Windows paths
# (backslashes) and values with spaces are rejected, and then the WHOLE file is ignored
# with only a warning. Forward-slash paths may stay unquoted.

# Yosys (OSS CAD Suite). Its bin\ and sibling lib\ are put first on PATH for the subprocess.
SVA2YOSYS_YOSYS='C:\opt\oss-cad-suite\bin\yosys.exe'
# SymbiYosys (bmc, prove, cover); solvers are taken from the same bin\ directory.
SVA2YOSYS_SBY='C:\opt\oss-cad-suite\bin\sby.exe'
# SymbiYosys with the suprove engine for liveness (Linux tool root), as a command split on
# whitespace and run in the work directory, e.g. through WSL.
SVA2YOSYS_SBY_LIVE='wsl -e /mnt/c/opt/oss-cad-suite-suprove-linux/bin/sby'

# EBMC (6.1, Linux binary) as a command split on whitespace and run in the work directory, e.g.
# through WSL (WSL sees the C: drive under /mnt/c). Used by the EBMC differential tier,
# tests/functional_tests/external/ebmc_differential; the version is checked by a test.
SVA2YOSYS_EBMC='wsl.exe -e /mnt/c/opt/ebmc/ebmc'
# The DIRECTORY that contains Spot's ltl2tgba (2.16.1, a Linux binary when EBMC runs through WSL).
# It is put first on the PATH of EBMC's process only (inside Linux when using WSL), where EBMC's
# --buechi finds the translator. Spot (GPL-3.0) is run as an external program, never linked.
SVA2YOSYS_LTL2TGBA='C:/opt/spot/bin'

# SystemVerilog slang executable (sv-lang, same version as the pyslang dependency); used only to
# cross-check that the exporter's JSON is a subset of Slang's native --ast-json output.
SVA2YOSYS_SLANG='C:\opt\slang\slang.exe'

# Verilator (mechanical interpretation probes). The shell runs builds; use MSYS bash on Windows
# or sh on POSIX. ROOT contains include/verilated.h. BUILD_PATH lists existing directories needed
# by the compiler, make and tool Python, separated by the platform path separator (semicolon on
# Windows, colon on POSIX). No tools are found through ambient PATH.
SVA2YOSYS_VERILATOR='C:/opt/verilator/bin/verilator.exe'
SVA2YOSYS_VERILATOR_SHELL='C:/msys64/usr/bin/bash.exe'
SVA2YOSYS_VERILATOR_ROOT='C:/opt/verilator'
SVA2YOSYS_VERILATOR_BUILD_PATH='C:/msys64/usr/bin;C:/opt/mingw64/bin;C:/opt/python'

# A checkout of the Yosys SVA tests (tests/sva of https://github.com/YosysHQ/yosys, ISC license),
# an external corpus that is not part of this repository; used by tests/functional_tests/external/yosys_corpus.
# Use an absolute path outside the repository (forward slashes). To fetch it (pinned commit):
#   uv run python tests/support/corpora.py C:/corpora yosys
SVA2YOSYS_YOSYS_SVA_TESTS='C:/corpora/yosys/tests/sva'

# A checkout of the EBMC regression tests (regression/verilog/SVA of https://github.com/diffblue/hw-cbmc,
# BSD-3-Clause), an external corpus that is not part of this repository; used by
# tests/functional_tests/external/ebmc_corpus. To fetch it:
#   uv run python tests/support/corpora.py C:/corpora ebmc
SVA2YOSYS_EBMC_TESTS='C:/corpora/ebmc/regression/verilog/SVA'

# A checkout of the SymbiYosys sources (docs/examples and tests of https://github.com/YosysHQ/sby,
# ISC), an external corpus that is not part of this repository; the variable names the checkout
# root. Used by tests/functional_tests/external/sby_examples. To fetch it:
#   uv run python tests/support/corpora.py C:/corpora sby
SVA2YOSYS_SBY_EXAMPLES='C:/corpora/sby'
